extends layout
include partials/pagehead

block content
  +pagehead("About Nash Luxury Realty", "We acquire, restore and hold industrial buildings.", "Nash Luxury Realty converts mills, warehouses and foundries in established districts into loft residences and creative office space, and offers them directly to buyers and tenants.", hero)

  section.band.page
    .detail-grid
      .prose
        h2 Acquisition
        p We buy buildings that can be converted without rebuilding the frame. The structural criteria are consistent: a frame capable of carrying residential or commercial floor loading, a column grid wide enough to leave open plan, and glazing on more than one elevation. Buildings that fail these tests produce small rooms and high costs, and we do not pursue them.
        p Acquisition is concentrated in a small number of districts in each of the nine cities we operate in. Repeat purchasing in the same area gives us established relationships with local authorities, contractors and consultants, which shortens programme and reduces risk on every subsequent conversion.
        h2 Restoration
        p A conversion takes between two and four years. Original structure is retained wherever consent and condition allow, including cast iron and timber framing, roof lights, crane beams and window openings. Building services, insulation, glazing performance and fire strategy are specified to current standards throughout.
        p Each project is delivered under the supervision of conservation officers where the building is listed or in a conservation area. Approved documentation is provided to purchasers and tenants in full.
        h2 Disposal
        p Completed buildings are offered for sale, on long lease, or on a corporate let, and in several cases on more than one basis at the same time. Nash Luxury Realty retains ownership of most of the portfolio and manages the buildings it lets.
        p Pricing, tenure, service charge, deposit and availability are published on each listing rather than provided on request.
      aside.aside
        h2 Dealing with the owner
        p Nash Luxury Realty owns every building it markets. There is no vendor chain and no separate agency acting between you and the information you need.
        p Survey findings, title documents, floor plates, load ratings and service charge history are held in this office and released in full to registered clients.
        a.button(href="/portfolio") View available properties
        a.button.button-quiet(href="/register") Register

  section.band.band-rule.band-raised
    .page
      .section-head
        div
          p.eyebrow Process
          h2 From enquiry to completion
      ol.steps
        li
          div
            h3 Register your requirement
            p Registration is reviewed within two working days. Approval opens exact addresses, full terms, floor plans and supporting documentation across the portfolio.
        li
          div
            h3 Receive detailed information
            p We provide floor plates, load ratings, energy performance certificates, service charge history and survey findings for any building under consideration.
        li
          div
            h3 View with the building manager
            p Viewings are arranged by appointment and accompanied by the member of staff responsible for the building.
        li
          div
            h3 Agree terms and complete
            p Reservation fees, holding deposits and first payments are taken only after written approval of your application, for a fixed amount, within a defined payment window.

  section.band.band-rule.page
    .stack
      h2 Register for early access to new releases
      p.lede Completed conversions are frequently reserved before they are advertised. Registered clients are notified first.
      .button-row
        a.button(href="/register") Register
        a.button.button-quiet(href="/contact") Contact us
